    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d50">

                <pb facs="0172" n="102" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg102"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Inquiry files</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Dr. Isaiah Bowman to Dr. S. E. Mezes </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-13">July 13,
                            1918</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Dr. Mezes</hi>: May I observe, in all respect,
                    that the state of affairs you point out in the attached memorandum<anchor n="19"
                        xml:id="d50-f1"/> is due to the <pb facs="0173" n="103" xml:id="pg103"/>
                    present loose organization of the Inquiry—possibly an excellent thing in a small
                    democratic organization but wholly inappropriate to a large one now establishing
                    broad relationships with almost every scientific bureau of the government.</p>
                <p>The time has come when there should be a stricter division of functions among the
                    officers of the Inquiry and an exact definition of status and appointments. It
                    is a source of growing embarrassment to remain as we are.</p>
                <p>Forgive my very direct and even blunt presentation of this matter. It saves time
                    and it is the way I like to speak.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Isaiah Bowman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
